# Challenge 1: Find the Highest Salary Employee

### Table

| id | name   | salary |
| -- | ------ | ------ |
| 1  | Akshay | 50000  |
| 2  | Rahul  | 80000  |
| 3  | Neha   | 70000  |

---

## First Thinking

Question asks:

```text
Highest salary
```

Not employee count.

Not grouping.

Need:

```text
Maximum value
```

---

## Query

```sql
SELECT *
FROM employees
WHERE salary =
(
   SELECT MAX(salary)
   FROM employees
);
```

---

## Why It Works

Step 1:

```sql
SELECT MAX(salary)
```

returns:

```text
80000
```

Step 2:

Find employee having 80000.

---

## Pattern

```text
Highest
Lowest
Maximum
Minimum
```

Think:

```text
MAX()
MIN()
```

