# Challenge 2: Find Departments Having More Than 5 Employees

---

## Thinking

Question contains:

```text
Per Department
```

Immediately:

```text
GROUP BY
```

---

## Query

```sql
SELECT department
FROM employees
GROUP BY department
HAVING COUNT(*) > 5;
```

---

## Why HAVING?

Remember:

```text
WHERE → rows

HAVING → groups
```

---

# Challenge 3: Find Employees Who Earn More Than Their Manager

---

## Tables

| emp_id | name | manager_id | salary |
| ------ | ---- | ---------- | ------ |

---

## Thinking

Need:

```text
Employee
vs
Manager
```

Same table.

---

## Pattern

```text
Same table comparison
```

Think:

```text
SELF JOIN
```

---

## Query

```sql
SELECT e.name
FROM employees e
JOIN employees m
ON e.manager_id = m.emp_id
WHERE e.salary > m.salary;
```

---

## Why It Works

Employee table acts twice:

```text
e → employee

m → manager
```

